@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container py-4 py-lg-5">
    <header class="rounded-4 bg-primary text-white p-4 p-lg-5 mb-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="row align-items-center g-3">
            <div class="col-lg-9">
                <span class="badge bg-light text-primary mb-2">ACXIOMCRM</span>
                <h1 class="display-6 fw-bold mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
                <p class="lead mb-0">How ACXIOMCRM handles account information and the customer and business records managed in the application.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-3 text-lg-end"><span class="badge rounded-pill text-bg-light">Application information</span></div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <div class="row g-4">
        <aside class="col-lg-3">
            <nav class="card border-0 shadow-sm sticky-lg-top" style="top: 1rem" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h2 class="h6 text-uppercase text-muted mb-3">On this page</h2>
                    <div class="list-group list-group-flush">
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action px-0" href="#purpose">Purpose</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action px-0" href="#information">Information collected</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action px-0" href="#use">How information is used</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action px-0" href="#security">Storage and security</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action px-0" href="#permissions">Access permissions</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action px-0" href="#sharing">Data sharing</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action px-0" href="#retention">Retention and deletion</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action px-0" href="#rights">Privacy requests</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action px-0" href="#cookies">Cookies</a>
                        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action px-0" href="#contact">Contact</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </nav>
        </aside>

        <main class="col-lg-9">
            <section id="purpose" class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h4">1. Introduction and purpose</h2>
                    <p class="mb-0">ACXIOMCRM is a customer relationship management application used to organize customer and lead records, follow-ups, sales opportunities, activities, reports, user accounts, and audit events. This page describes the information the application handles and the controls implemented in its current configuration. The organization operating this installation may have additional policies for its deployment and data practices.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="information" class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h4">2. Information collected</h2>
                    <p>Information entered into or generated by ACXIOMCRM can include:</p>
                    <ul class="mb-0">
                        <li><strong>Account information:</strong> name, email address, phone number when provided, account status, role, team assignment, and authentication data maintained by ASP.NET Core Identity.</li>
                        <li><strong>Customer and lead information:</strong> names, email addresses, phone numbers, company names, addresses, locations, lead sources and statuses, assigned employees, and record dates.</li>
                        <li><strong>Sales and work records:</strong> opportunity titles, amounts, stages, probabilities and expected close dates; follow-up subjects, descriptions, scheduled dates and statuses; activity subjects, descriptions, dates, statuses, priorities, and related CRM records.</li>
                        <li><strong>Security and audit information:</strong> account sign-in events and records of successful create, update, and delete actions, including the user, module, time, and brief action details.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="use" class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h4">3. How information is used</h2>
                    <p class="mb-0">ACXIOMCRM uses this information to provide CRM features: displaying and maintaining customer and lead records, assigning work, managing follow-ups and activities, tracking opportunities, preparing reports, authenticating users, applying permissions, and recording audit events. The application does not need a user's plaintext password to perform these functions.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="security" class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h4">4. Data storage and security</h2>
                    <p>CRM and Identity records are stored in the MySQL database configured for this installation. ASP.NET Core Identity hashes passwords for verification; the application does not store passwords in readable form. Authentication uses an Identity cookie.</p>
                    <ul class="mb-0">
                        <li>The authentication cookie is marked HttpOnly and SameSite Lax. It is configured to require HTTPS outside Development mode.</li>
                        <li>The configured authentication cookie expires after eight hours and uses sliding expiration.</li>
                        <li>Role and module permission checks are enforced on the server, with record-level scoping for assigned and team records.</li>
                        <li>Account lockout is configured after repeated unsuccessful sign-in attempts.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="text-muted small mt-3 mb-0">Security also depends on how the installation, database, backups, keys, hosting, and administrator accounts are managed. No software can guarantee absolute security.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="permissions" class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h4">5. User access permissions</h2>
                    <p>Access is controlled by assigned Identity roles and module permissions:</p>
                    <div class="row g-3">
                        <div class="col-md-4"><div class="h-100 rounded-3 border p-3"><h3 class="h6 text-primary">Admin</h3><p class="small mb-0">Can administer users and roles and has full CRM module access, including audit logs.</p></div></div>
                        <div class="col-md-4"><div class="h-100 rounded-3 border p-3"><h3 class="h6 text-primary">Manager</h3><p class="small mb-0">Has permissions granted to the Manager role and access to team-scoped CRM records.</p></div></div>
                        <div class="col-md-4"><div class="h-100 rounded-3 border p-3"><h3 class="h6 text-primary">SalesExecutive</h3><p class="small mb-0">Has permissions granted to the SalesExecutive role and access scoped to assigned CRM records.</p></div></div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="small text-muted mt-3 mb-0">An administrator can configure role permissions. Access may therefore vary by installation and role configuration.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="sharing" class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h4">6. Data sharing and third-party services</h2>
                    <p>ACXIOMCRM stores application records in the configured MySQL database. The application code does not implement an automatic advertising or marketing data-sharing service. Database, hosting, backup, or other service operators selected by the organization may process or access data as part of operating this installation.</p>
                    <p class="mb-0">The Dashboard and Reports pages load Chart.js from jsDelivr. A browser viewing those pages requests the script from that CDN, which may receive standard request information such as the browser's network address. The chart data is rendered in the page; the application does not send report records to the CDN as a chart API. Other services may apply if the operator configures integrations outside the application.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="retention" class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h4">7. Data retention and deletion</h2>
                    <p class="mb-0">The application has no automatic retention period configured for CRM records or audit logs. Records remain in the configured database until removed through an authorized application operation or by the database operator. Audit logs are available to Admins and are not removed by the Audit Logs page. Backups and their retention are managed by the organization operating the database and hosting environment.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="rights" class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h4">8. Privacy requests and data protection</h2>
                    <p class="mb-0">If you need to review or correct information, or request an account change or deletion, contact the administrator for your ACXIOMCRM installation. The administrator can review requests and determine the appropriate action under the organization's policies and any requirements that apply to it. Access to records is limited by the account's role, module permissions, and record assignment.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="cookies" class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h4">9. Cookies and session management</h2>
                    <p class="mb-0">After sign-in, ACXIOMCRM uses the <code>.ACXIOMCRM.Auth</code> authentication cookie to maintain the session. The cookie is HttpOnly, uses SameSite Lax, and is configured for HTTPS in non-Development environments. Sessions expire after eight hours, with sliding expiration. Signing out removes the authenticated session. The application does not configure a separate analytics or advertising cookie.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="contact" class="card border-0 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h4">10. Contact for privacy questions</h2>
                    <p class="mb-0">For questions about information in this ACXIOMCRM installation, contact the administrator or support contact designated by your organization. Contact details are not published here because they depend on the organization operating the installation.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <p class="small text-muted mt-3 mb-0">This page describes the application's current features and configuration. The operating organization should review it against its own deployment and policies.</p>
        </main>
    </div>
</div>
